      "writtenOn": "2015-04-20T00:41:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "where is Resource_dirs?\nNote that we have two types of resources:\nLOCAL_JAVA_RESOURCE_DIRS, LOCAL_JAVA_RESOURCE_FILES: resources common to all Java modules. (i.e., files to be added to the jar file)\nLOCAL_RESOURCE_DIR: Android resource compiled and packaged to apk by aapt.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 57,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 57,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "8737e1e5d06cd1d5570c958c3d632b53b6ad5d3c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d0435e7f_a157d8e0",
        "filename": "java/app.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-04-20T01:47:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Resource_dirs is inherited from the javaBase one.  Do we need to support LOCAL_JAVA_RESOURCE_DIRS in an app?  I just reused it to be an aapt resource dir if it is an app, or a java resource dir if it is a library.  A quick search didn\u0027t find any BUILD_PACKAGE modules with LOCAL_JAVA_RESOURCE_DIRS set, but I didn\u0027t do a thorough check.",
      "parentUuid": "f03ce2f3_c2414419",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 57,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 57,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "8737e1e5d06cd1d5570c958c3d632b53b6ad5d3c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d06c3e17_60c93b2c",
        "filename": "java/app.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003981
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-04-20T17:52:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, we do need LOCAL_JAVA_RESOURCE_DIRS in app.\nActually we used to forbid LOCAL_JAVA_RESOURCE_DIRS in app, but then requirement emerged when an app used third-party library (IIRC, it\u0027s an unbundled app), and we found no reason to forbid it.\n(P.S. I found the bug 6892294.)",
      "parentUuid": "d0435e7f_a157d8e0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 57,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 57,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "8737e1e5d06cd1d5570c958c3d632b53b6ad5d3c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f055c239_ec90afc8",
        "filename": "java/app.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-04-20T18:03:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think resources in static java libraries should already work, because I start with the jarFile produced by javaBase which already includes resources+classes.dex, then add the aapt resources to it.\n\nAs a non-java developer, JAVA_RESOURCE_DIRS vs. RESOURCE_DIRS is already confusing, and it seems simpler to have resource_dirs property that does what you expect for a java library and for an android app.  If that\u0027s not possible, then maybe java_resource_dirs and app_resource_dirs would be a little clearer, as well as some documentation on what the difference is.",
      "parentUuid": "d06c3e17_60c93b2c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 57,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 57,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "8737e1e5d06cd1d5570c958c3d632b53b6ad5d3c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f055c239_e03b9349",
        "filename": "java/app.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003981
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-04-20T18:34:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It may be reasonable to disallow apk with its own Java resources, in the spirit of replacing them with Android resources.\nBut for static Java libraries, I think both Java resources and Android resources are in active use. To support Android resource for static java library is another story, see http://b/issue?id\u003d5714516.\nI think we need to distinguish these two resources. java_resource_dirs v.s. app_resource_dirs ( android_resource_dirs may be better) sounds good to me.",
      "parentUuid": "f055c239_ec90afc8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 57,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 57,
        "endChar": 21
      },
