      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-04-20T01:47:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Allowing random rules to generate into the same directory causes dependency problems that lead to cleanspecs, because they might leave old files there and we would have no way to know to remove them.  I use a separate directory for every rule, and then pass the filelist to whatever javac command is used to compile it with @filelist.",
      "parentUuid": "f03ce2f3_82d3bcd7",
